{"Title":"An Act relative to acute hospital governance","BillNumber":"S1404","DocketNumber":"SD292","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T18:01:16.697"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T18:01:16.6966667"},{"Id":"RLR0","Name":"Rebecca L. Rausch","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RLR0","ResponseDate":"2023-07-11T11:19:16.9566667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1404/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Lovely, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1404) of Joan B. Lovely for legislation relative to acute hospital governance.  Public Health.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 51 of Chapter 111 is hereby amended by adding at the end thereof the following new paragraph:-\r\n\tAll acute-care hospitals as defined in section twenty-five B, shall have a registered nurse holding a current unencumbered license from the board of registration in nursing as a sitting and voting member of the governing entity responsible for developing the organization’s strategic plan, structure, systems, policies and programs.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J16","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J16"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}